WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.031 --> 00:00:05.457
Aunt Judy hated vacuuming.

2
00:00:05.458 --> 00:00:10.960
"This vacuum cleaner is too heavy," she said.

3
00:00:10.961 --> 00:00:14.041
"And it's too loud."

4
00:00:14.042 --> 00:00:20.243
"You need a robot vacuum," Harry said.

5
00:00:20.244 --> 00:00:24.640
Aunt Judy was delighted when the new vacuum arrived.

6
00:00:24.641 --> 00:00:29.852
"You're the robot expert," she said to Harry.

7
00:00:29.853 --> 00:00:35.249
"So, you're in charge."

8
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.834
"Okay," Harry said.

9
00:00:38.836 --> 00:00:42.817
He turned on the vacuum.

10
00:00:42.818 --> 00:00:50.452
"Woof! Woof!" Rover chased after it.

11
00:00:50.453 --> 00:00:55.416
Harry put Rover in the kitchen.

12
00:00:55.417 --> 00:01:02.843
"Help!" Emmy cried. "The robot is eating my socks!"

13
00:01:02.844 --> 00:01:13.351
Harry raced to help Aunt Judy rescue Emmy's socks.

14
00:01:13.352 --> 00:01:17.926
The robot bumped one of Oliver's cars.

15
00:01:17.927 --> 00:01:23.451
It backed up, stopped, and bumped the car again.

16
00:01:23.453 --> 00:01:31.328
Oliver laughed. "It doesn't know what to do!"

17
00:01:31.329 --> 00:01:42.291
"Take everything off the floor," Harry said.

18
00:01:42.292 --> 00:01:45.757
"I'll make the robot listen and talk."

19
00:01:45.758 --> 00:01:48.987
He pushed some buttons.

20
00:01:48.988 --> 00:01:52.916
"Hello!" the robot suddenly shouted.

21
00:01:52.917 --> 00:01:57.996
"That's too loud!" Emmy covered her ears.

22
00:01:57.997 --> 00:02:02.686
"I'm turning left!" the robot announced.

23
00:02:02.687 --> 00:02:08.661
"I'm turning right!

24
00:02:08.662 --> 00:02:12.351
I'm under the couch!"

25
00:02:12.352 --> 00:02:16.332
Harry couldn't lower the volume.

26
00:02:16.333 --> 00:02:21.508
He couldn't make the robot stop talking.

27
00:02:21.509 --> 00:02:27.293
"Turn that thing off!" Aunt Judy cried.

28
00:02:27.295 --> 00:02:33.257
"I can't!" Harry said.

29
00:02:33.258 --> 00:02:38.622
"Then put it outside," she said.

30
00:02:38.623 --> 00:02:45.794
"It's worse than the old vacuum!"

31
00:02:45.795 --> 00:02:49.314
Later the kids looked outside.

32
00:02:49.315 --> 00:02:52.516
Emmy and Oliver laughed.

33
00:02:52.517 --> 00:02:57.385
"Aunt Judy, there's a problem," Harry called.

34
00:02:57.386 --> 00:03:05.791
"The robot is running away!"

